  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Brady Basso lasted four innings, and the bullpen held everything after that. A 2\u20130 grind where nothing came easy and nothing broke.",
    "what_this_means": "The offense got exactly what it needed from Max Muncy, who went 2-for-2 and gave them the only run they could find. The bullpen did the rest. Scott Blewett threw two clean innings, Luis Medina struck out two in one, Hogan Harris kept it tight in the eighth, and Elvis Alvarado finished it with two strikeouts in the ninth. They never led by more than two. They never trailed. They just stayed ahead long enough for that margin to hold. This isn't about brilliance. This is about one run standing up when the bullpen doesn't blink. That's the only way you win 2\u20130 games.",
    "what_to_watch": "Seattle comes to town tomorrow with a .229 average, the kind of matchup Jeffrey Springs should control if the bullpen stays in this shape.",
